<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕlĕphantĭnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		elephas. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Belonging to the elephant</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tergum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					1, 5, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλεφάντινος</span>, pure Lat.
			eburnĕus, <i>of ivory</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liber,</span>”
				<i>consisting of ivory tablets</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Tacit. 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">atramentum,</span>”
				<i>ivoryblack</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 6, 25, § 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compositio (emplastri),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 5, 19, 24</span></i>
			 Daremb.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
